{
  "case_id": "2009-08-586",
  "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 1970, Congress amended the Investment Company Act to provide a cause of action when an investment adviser breaches its fiduciary duty with respect to compensation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And, third, applying that standard here, Harris charged twice as much in percentage terms for providing virtually identical advisory services in arm's-length transactions with institutional investors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The recovery inures to the entire benefit of all the investors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Curtis E. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0000-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The fiduciary duty imposed by section 36(b) prohibits an investment adviser's fee from being outside the range that arm's-length bargaining would produce."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, even under this statute, the SEC has the authority to file suits under section 36(b)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Well, it must be aware of the -- of the divergence between the fees that investment advisers charge to these companies and what they charge to other clients. Isn't the SEC aware of that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It has used less formal mechanisms in the context of examinations and investigators --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John Bogel",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the 1969 memorandum that I referred to, which is reprinted in an appendix to the amicus brief by John Bogel in its entirety, the SEC mentioned that comparison as being something that may well be relevant in proving in an individual case that that particular investment adviser's fees are excessive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Gannon, the -- all the circumstances, that comes from the Second Circuit's Gartenberg case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Solicitor General",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe they interpret in the Gartenberg sense. I think that the Solicitor General's position and the Respondent's, with respect to the standard that you ought to apply, is Gartenberg."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would -- would you give us the citations of the parts of the record that you say render it unnecessary for us to remand for the lower court to consider a comparison with non- -- with institutional charges?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the petitioners' allegation that the investment adviser did not provide full and accurate information? And they mention particularly concerning economies of scale, profitability, and several other matters, that what everybody agrees is necessary, full disclosure, had not occurred."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ostensible misrepresentations on -- among other things, profitability and the rest, this was because the plaintiffs' expert did an accounting and accounted for costs differently and said, had you accounted for costs and allocated them the way I did, you would have reached a negotiated result that was different."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-586",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "bc586594721bd7bdf1b7a622ddc4c44cac7fab2e248290ae24e8992c398ec8c1",
      "evidence_id": "ev-bc586594721b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
